    "body": "Investigation (issue-worker-high):\n\n**Where the rotation comes from.**\n- `LocatePart` moves the part with `MoveModel::locating`. The stock follows the part rigidly in `MoveModel::build` (`crates/app/src/commands/move_model.rs`).\n- The locate solve (`fixture_locate_solve.rs`) reads normals from mesh faces. Its result rotation has float noise (about 1e-13 to 1e-16) when the part has a turn.\n- `turns()` reads a change of 1e-12 or less as \"no turn\". Thus `keep_square` does not run, and the rigid-follow branch writes the noise rotation into the stock `Location`.\n- `stock_fit` keeps the stock rotation when the stock is fitted again. Thus the noise stays in the project.\n- `stock_view::stock_facets` and `stock_sim::stock_grid` refuse each rotation that is not exactly `IDENTITY_Q`. A noise rotation of 5e-14 is refused.\n- A probe test reproduces it: a part with a rotation of 1e-13 rad, located in a vise, gives a stock rotation of `[0,0,-5e-14,1]` and the refusal.\n- A second case: a \"from model\" stock that follows a quarter turn of its part carries a true quarter-turn rotation. The sim also refuses it today.\n\n**What verify does for this stock.**\n- `posting_sim` cannot simulate the stock. The post result, the status line and the G-code header show the line \"stock sim did not judge this program: <reason>\". The line is always visible.\n- The generator-time verify of each operation still runs. It judges each toolpath against the part and the fixtures. Its warnings block the post.\n- The post is blocked when an operation has no fresh generator-time verify verdict.\n- Thus the output is not silent. The refusal is visible and the per-operation checks stay in force. The priority stays P3.\n\n**Plan.**\n1. Stop the noise at its source: a stock that follows a move with no turn keeps its own rotation.\n2. One law for the simulation frame: a rotation that is a quarter-turn multiple (within 1e-9) is modelled as its axis-aligned box. An oblique stock stays refused.\n3. The refusal text becomes plain English, shows one time, and the stock stays visible.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
